  "details": "When curl is built with GnuTLS, a malicious WebSocket server can make curl\nsend memory past its send buffer. This is due to an out of bounds read\nfollowing when `gnutls_record_send()` returns a number of bytes sent **greater\nthan the number of bytes it was given to send**. GnuTLS does that after a\nblocked send.",
